WEBVTT

1
00:00:12,947 --> 00:00:16,049
[rain pattering]

2
00:00:17,986 --> 00:00:22,356
[thunder rumbling]

3
00:00:29,898 --> 00:00:31,098
[dog whimpers]

4
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:34,134
[opera music playing in the
background]

5
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:36,470
[bird squawks]

6
00:00:38,138 --> 00:00:40,642
-[thunder booms]
-[bird squawks]

7
00:00:40,675 --> 00:00:43,811
[opera music continues]

8
00:01:03,163 --> 00:01:04,799
[bird squawking]

9
00:01:09,136 --> 00:01:11,873
[dog whimpering]

10
00:01:11,906 --> 00:01:13,741
[thunder rumbling]

11
00:01:14,742 --> 00:01:15,743
[bird squawks]

12
00:01:17,745 --> 00:01:19,479
[thunder booms]

13
00:01:20,582 --> 00:01:24,052
[opera music continues]

14
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:40,200
[thunder rumbles]

15
00:01:50,444 --> 00:01:51,713
[knocking]

16
00:01:51,746 --> 00:01:52,680
[Marcos] Come in.

17
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:54,381
[door opens]

18
00:01:54,983 --> 00:01:56,751
[Kostas] I'm sorry, sir.

19
00:01:56,784 --> 00:01:58,519
Something has happened.

20
00:02:00,922 --> 00:02:02,456
It's about your son.

21
00:02:07,361 --> 00:02:11,966
[radio chattering in foreign
language]

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,102
[rain pattering]

23
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,837
[radio chattering in foreign
language]

24
00:02:21,075 --> 00:02:23,544
[footsteps approaching]

25
00:02:29,550 --> 00:02:30,551
[Kostas] Sir.

26
00:02:31,786 --> 00:02:32,787
We found him.

27
00:02:36,958 --> 00:02:38,693
Marcos, I'm so sorry.

28
00:02:45,033 --> 00:02:46,834
[lighter flicks]

29
00:02:48,603 --> 00:02:53,273
[somber music]

30
00:02:58,913 --> 00:03:00,615
[Marcos] Just leave me alone.

31
00:03:11,224 --> 00:03:13,828
[somber music intensifies]

32
00:03:39,687 --> 00:03:41,354
[wind blowing]

33
00:03:44,859 --> 00:03:46,894
[birds chirping]

34
00:03:54,836 --> 00:03:57,004
[waves lapping]

35
00:03:59,674 --> 00:04:00,641
[men chattering]

36
00:04:00,675 --> 00:04:01,743
[Marcos] <i>Sofia,</i>

37
00:04:02,944 --> 00:04:04,244
<i>my little girl.</i>

38
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:08,950
<i>I am here at our house,</i>
<i>writing my thoughts</i>

39
00:04:08,983 --> 00:04:12,720
<i>just before everyone arrives</i>
<i>for your party.</i>

40
00:04:13,988 --> 00:04:16,624
<i>I've missed you so much.</i>

41
00:04:16,657 --> 00:04:19,994
<i>I want you to know that I don't</i>
<i>like what I have to do,</i>

42
00:04:20,762 --> 00:04:22,262
<i>but I have to do it.</i>

43
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,264
[chattering]

44
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:26,366
<i>I'm sure you'll understand,</i>

45
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:30,571
<i>that you'll agree</i>
<i>with me in the end.</i>

46
00:04:30,605 --> 00:04:35,009
<i>We'll do what needs to be done,</i>
<i>and we'll carry on.</i>

47
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:37,912
<i>That's what a family does best.</i>

48
00:04:39,013 --> 00:04:40,982
<i>That's what makes us special.</i>

49
00:04:41,916 --> 00:04:44,585
<i>Can't wait to put my arms</i>
<i>around you.</i>

50
00:04:45,418 --> 00:04:48,856
[gentle music playing]

51
00:04:51,092 --> 00:04:52,492
[curtains open]

52
00:04:53,161 --> 00:04:55,963
[footsteps approaching]

53
00:04:55,997 --> 00:05:00,400
[gentle music continues,
singing in foreign language]

54
00:05:15,382 --> 00:05:16,383
[telephone rings]

55
00:05:16,416 --> 00:05:18,019
[Marcos speaking
foreign language]

56
00:05:19,987 --> 00:05:21,088
[telephone clicks]

57
00:05:21,122 --> 00:05:22,389
[tape recorder starts]

58
00:05:22,422 --> 00:05:25,259
[Marcos] I said I wasn't
available for anyone today.

59
00:05:25,293 --> 00:05:26,227
[man on phone] Yes, sir.

60
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:27,662
But it's really important.

61
00:05:29,597 --> 00:05:32,332
[Marcos] Just tell me
where they are.

62
00:05:32,365 --> 00:05:35,536
-29 North, 33 East.
-[water faucet running]

63
00:05:35,570 --> 00:05:37,404
They're already right there.

64
00:05:38,206 --> 00:05:39,273
No, no.

65
00:05:39,307 --> 00:05:41,642
Tell Stavros there's
no turning back.

66
00:05:43,177 --> 00:05:44,712
That's just rumors.

67
00:05:44,745 --> 00:05:48,115
Listen, we [chuckles] we are
the fucking pirates.

68
00:05:48,149 --> 00:05:49,784
Just write down what I say.

69
00:05:50,985 --> 00:05:54,222
Stavros crossed today
or never come back.

70
00:05:54,255 --> 00:05:56,691
I know the pass is clean.

71
00:05:56,724 --> 00:05:59,794
Don't listen to anyone, Marcos.

72
00:05:59,827 --> 00:06:01,929
Send me a telex
with his position,

73
00:06:01,963 --> 00:06:03,064
after they have crossed.

74
00:06:03,097 --> 00:06:06,399
-[gentle music continues]
-[tape recorder stops]

75
00:06:10,504 --> 00:06:12,840
[dog whimpers, barks]

76
00:06:15,209 --> 00:06:16,677
Good morning my boy.

77
00:06:18,112 --> 00:06:19,479
The bath is ready sir.

78
00:06:20,014 --> 00:06:21,381
Thank you, Marisa.

79
00:06:22,750 --> 00:06:24,719
[Marcos speaking
foreign language]

80
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:28,522
[footsteps receding]

81
00:06:30,457 --> 00:06:33,393
[Marcos] Run down to her.
Take Icarus with you.

82
00:06:33,426 --> 00:06:35,062
[dog panting]

83
00:06:35,096 --> 00:06:39,000
[radio static, chattering]

84
00:06:47,174 --> 00:06:48,943
<i>-It's an honor.</i>
<i>-Welcome sir.</i>

85
00:06:48,976 --> 00:06:51,712
<i>-Very nice to see you again.</i>
<i>-Nice to see you too.</i>

86
00:06:52,613 --> 00:06:55,549
<i>-Carlos. I don't believe it.</i>
<i>-Hi.</i>

87
00:06:55,583 --> 00:06:57,952
[indistinct chattering]

88
00:06:58,886 --> 00:07:01,389
<i>Thank you, Jack.</i>

89
00:07:01,421 --> 00:07:04,091
[upbeat music playing]

90
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:07,595
[boat engine revving]

91
00:07:14,769 --> 00:07:18,673
<i>Master's orders, no commercial</i>
<i>allowed on the island.</i>

92
00:07:18,706 --> 00:07:20,675
Your daughter looks beautiful.

93
00:07:21,474 --> 00:07:22,543
Hello, Kostas.

94
00:07:22,576 --> 00:07:26,047
[indistinct chatter]

95
00:07:29,116 --> 00:07:32,086
[party guests] Woo, woo!

96
00:07:32,119 --> 00:07:34,522
[speedboat roars]

97
00:07:40,493 --> 00:07:42,863
[Marisa] Sofia!
Sofia.

98
00:07:43,431 --> 00:07:46,233
[radio static]

99
00:07:47,234 --> 00:07:51,639
[dramatic music]

100
00:08:09,523 --> 00:08:11,726
[birds chirping]

101
00:08:27,341 --> 00:08:28,809
I'm so sorry, sir.

102
00:08:31,645 --> 00:08:33,647
I... It's because of the baby.

103
00:08:33,681 --> 00:08:35,149
We don't sleep well at night.

104
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:37,051
-Yanis, right?
-Yeah.

105
00:08:37,084 --> 00:08:38,285
Yes, sir.

106
00:08:38,319 --> 00:08:39,387
She's Yanis.

107
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:40,955
She's a month-old today,
Mr. Marcos.

108
00:08:41,355 --> 00:08:42,590
It's okay.

109
00:08:42,623 --> 00:08:45,226
I know it's hard at first,
but tuck in your shirt

110
00:08:45,259 --> 00:08:46,427
and get your shit together.

111
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:48,129
Thank you, sir.
It won't happen again.

112
00:08:48,162 --> 00:08:49,230
[Marcos] Of course it won't.

113
00:08:50,564 --> 00:08:51,899
[door opens, closes]

114
00:08:53,167 --> 00:08:54,402
Impressive, Marcos.

115
00:08:54,435 --> 00:08:55,603
Congratulations.

116
00:08:55,636 --> 00:08:58,639
It's an exact copy of a room
at Mount Sinai.

117
00:08:58,672 --> 00:09:00,141
Even a little better, maybe.

118
00:09:01,609 --> 00:09:03,577
Is there something I don't
know, dear?

119
00:09:03,611 --> 00:09:06,447
No, I'm fine, don't worry.

120
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:08,616
It's just
that I don't want to entrust

121
00:09:08,649 --> 00:09:12,653
everything to a damn Greek army
helicopter, that's all.

122
00:09:12,686 --> 00:09:14,989
I feel safer with all this here.

123
00:09:15,823 --> 00:09:21,228
And I also still
have my flare gun.

124
00:09:21,262 --> 00:09:22,596
[laughing]

125
00:09:26,535 --> 00:09:27,968
Come on.

126
00:09:28,002 --> 00:09:32,773
I'd feel much better if I put
some of this equipment on you.

127
00:09:32,807 --> 00:09:36,143
You're the only man I ever let
unbutton my shirt.

128
00:09:39,447 --> 00:09:42,817
Don't tell Sofia
about any of this.

129
00:09:42,850 --> 00:09:46,053
I don't want her to worry
for no reason.

130
00:09:46,954 --> 00:09:48,355
As you wish.

131
00:09:48,389 --> 00:09:51,560
I saw her a moment ago
on the pier.

132
00:09:51,592 --> 00:09:55,796
She looked beautiful
and wild like her father.

133
00:09:56,565 --> 00:10:00,000
Sofia, 25 already, unbelievable.

134
00:10:00,034 --> 00:10:02,670
It's not easy being your
daughter, you know.

135
00:10:04,738 --> 00:10:06,740
Okay, let's see.

136
00:10:10,579 --> 00:10:11,580
Breathe.

137
00:10:11,612 --> 00:10:13,714
[inhaling]

138
00:10:13,747 --> 00:10:15,749
And let the air out slowly.

139
00:10:16,217 --> 00:10:18,819
[exhaling]

140
00:10:19,186 --> 00:10:20,154
Okay.

141
00:10:23,124 --> 00:10:26,293
Daniel would be 28 now.

142
00:10:26,327 --> 00:10:29,598
[somber music]

143
00:10:29,630 --> 00:10:31,732
He'd be boss
of 10,000 employees,

144
00:10:31,765 --> 00:10:33,834
and I'd be able
to start resting.

145
00:10:35,136 --> 00:10:36,103
Finally.

146
00:10:39,473 --> 00:10:40,975
I'm fine, Patrick.

147
00:10:42,309 --> 00:10:43,344
Really, my friend.

148
00:10:44,145 --> 00:10:45,246
Thank you for coming.

149
00:10:46,313 --> 00:10:48,883
I don't like the sound of your
right clunk.

150
00:10:48,916 --> 00:10:52,219
But at the end of the day,
if you don't destroy yourself,

151
00:10:52,253 --> 00:10:53,721
no one will.

152
00:10:58,759 --> 00:11:00,161
[Marisa] How have you been?

153
00:11:02,196 --> 00:11:04,265
You've been gone
for too many years.

154
00:11:04,298 --> 00:11:05,766
How have you been?

155
00:11:05,799 --> 00:11:08,435
[Sofia] Come on! [chuckling]

156
00:11:08,469 --> 00:11:10,505
Just been gone for four years.

157
00:11:10,539 --> 00:11:12,273
Well, I missed you.

158
00:11:13,741 --> 00:11:15,409
I missed you, too.

159
00:11:22,883 --> 00:11:26,287
How are you?
Like, how is it all going here?

160
00:11:28,055 --> 00:11:30,057
Well, you know.

161
00:11:30,090 --> 00:11:33,194
I mean, the first few days,
it's like a paradise.

162
00:11:33,227 --> 00:11:37,464
But any longer
than that, it feels like a cage.

163
00:11:37,498 --> 00:11:38,465
So...

164
00:11:41,068 --> 00:11:41,802
Yeah.

165
00:11:41,835 --> 00:11:43,070
But I'm good.

166
00:11:43,971 --> 00:11:46,040
Better than ever, maybe.

167
00:11:47,708 --> 00:11:49,109
[man] Marisa!

168
00:11:49,743 --> 00:11:51,546
[Marisa] Fuck.

169
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:54,782
I have to go
or my father will kill me.

170
00:11:54,815 --> 00:11:56,150
Or my father would kill you.

171
00:11:56,183 --> 00:11:58,953
Oh, yeah, well, I'd rather
have my father kill me.

172
00:11:58,986 --> 00:12:06,727
Anyway, listen, why don't you
take me with you when you leave?

173
00:12:07,596 --> 00:12:09,330
Yeah, you wanna come?

174
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,335
See you.

175
00:12:30,884 --> 00:12:32,353
[recording tape plays]

176
00:12:32,987 --> 00:12:34,288
[Sofia on recording] <i>Hi.</i>

177
00:12:35,256 --> 00:12:36,857
<i>No, I'm in London.</i>

178
00:12:37,692 --> 00:12:38,993
<i>Yes.</i>

179
00:12:39,927 --> 00:12:41,962
<i>[chuckling] It's a safe line.</i>

180
00:12:43,497 --> 00:12:44,999
<i>Yeah.</i>

181
00:12:45,032 --> 00:12:46,934
<i>And you'll have to accept it.</i>

182
00:12:46,967 --> 00:12:51,338
[recorder rewinding]

183
00:12:53,207 --> 00:12:55,042
<i>[chuckling] It's a safe line.</i>

184
00:12:56,377 --> 00:12:57,344
<i>Yeah.</i>

185
00:12:58,747 --> 00:13:00,447
<i>And you'll have to accept it.</i>

186
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:04,251
<i>I'm gonna go all the way</i>
<i>with this baby.</i>

187
00:13:04,285 --> 00:13:06,420
[recorder rewinding]

188
00:13:08,523 --> 00:13:10,090
<i>Go all the way with this baby.</i>

189
00:13:10,659 --> 00:13:12,126
<i>My time has come.</i>

190
00:13:15,664 --> 00:13:20,568
[record plays upbeat music]

191
00:13:27,274 --> 00:13:28,777
[water splashing]

192
00:13:28,809 --> 00:13:32,046
[guests chattering]

193
00:13:46,894 --> 00:13:51,165
[woman singing in foreign
language]

194
00:13:59,808 --> 00:14:02,510
Now Patrick, you're going to
have to excuse me.

195
00:14:02,544 --> 00:14:03,911
Okay, Marcos.

196
00:14:07,948 --> 00:14:10,618
Great Timoleon, my friend.

197
00:14:10,652 --> 00:14:11,753
[laughing]

198
00:14:11,786 --> 00:14:13,621
How are yo so, long time.

199
00:14:15,255 --> 00:14:17,991
I'm so sorry my wife
couldn't come.

200
00:14:18,025 --> 00:14:20,494
She stayed in the palace taking
care of her father.

201
00:14:21,462 --> 00:14:23,665
Anyway, I'm going to
introduce you, Olga,

202
00:14:23,698 --> 00:14:25,232
my personal assistant.

203
00:14:25,265 --> 00:14:27,134
It's a great pleasure
to meet you.

204
00:14:27,836 --> 00:14:29,604
How is General Franco?

205
00:14:31,405 --> 00:14:32,507
[clicks tongue]

206
00:14:33,575 --> 00:14:35,510
Where is your daughter, Sofia?

207
00:14:35,543 --> 00:14:36,443
You tell me.

208
00:14:36,477 --> 00:14:39,146
[all laughing]

209
00:14:40,615 --> 00:14:42,517
Still working, Mr. Forster.

210
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:44,586
Patrikios.

211
00:14:46,453 --> 00:14:48,288
-Good to see you.
-Good to see you too.

212
00:14:48,322 --> 00:14:51,024
[Forster] Yeah, this was
just a few days ago.

213
00:14:51,058 --> 00:14:53,961
I wonder if the marquis came
for more than just the party.

214
00:14:53,994 --> 00:14:55,663
You are the expert here.

215
00:14:57,799 --> 00:14:59,634
Who is this Englishman
over there?

216
00:15:00,769 --> 00:15:04,438
[indistinct chatter]

217
00:15:04,471 --> 00:15:05,607
He's nobody.

218
00:15:07,007 --> 00:15:08,275
There he is.

219
00:15:08,308 --> 00:15:11,011
-Our Champion, my boy, Carlos.
-Marcos.

220
00:15:11,044 --> 00:15:13,046
-How are you?
-How are you?

221
00:15:13,848 --> 00:15:17,852
[speaking foreign language]

222
00:15:17,886 --> 00:15:20,154
[Marcos laughing] Bravo.

223
00:15:20,187 --> 00:15:23,290
My friends, excuse me, I must
go greet my wife.

224
00:15:23,323 --> 00:15:25,025
I'm looking forward
to meeting her.

225
00:15:25,058 --> 00:15:26,895
I'm such a fan of the signora.

226
00:15:26,927 --> 00:15:29,029
Of course, Olga, of course.

227
00:15:29,062 --> 00:15:31,599
Right now, I'll tell her to come
over and say hello.

228
00:15:31,633 --> 00:15:32,933
Thank you.

229
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:42,777
Forster, come with me
to my office.

230
00:15:42,811 --> 00:15:47,147
[background music
continues playing]

231
00:15:56,089 --> 00:15:59,092
Well, we should've
seen that coming.

232
00:15:59,126 --> 00:16:02,129
We all know what
Marcos is like.

233
00:16:02,162 --> 00:16:06,467
The wealthy bourgeoisie is our
irreconcilable enemy.

234
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:09,470
His wealth is founded
on our poverty.

235
00:16:11,639 --> 00:16:12,740
Stalin.

236
00:16:14,007 --> 00:16:17,010
A declared enemy is always
much easier to fight.

237
00:16:18,646 --> 00:16:24,218
You know, they've already made
a movie about me, Forster.

238
00:16:24,251 --> 00:16:26,153
You mean "The Godfather?"

239
00:16:26,186 --> 00:16:29,122
No, it's about a big shark.

240
00:16:30,424 --> 00:16:32,727
Surprised to see the fascist
marquis here.

241
00:16:35,062 --> 00:16:36,363
Have a seat.

242
00:16:37,565 --> 00:16:41,736
Never judge a man who makes
business with another man.

243
00:16:44,137 --> 00:16:46,173
Aren't you doing business
with me?

244
00:16:48,175 --> 00:16:50,377
By the way, I haven't read it.

245
00:16:54,214 --> 00:16:56,416
I've been working on this for
two years.

246
00:16:56,450 --> 00:16:58,987
It's your life
we're talking about.

247
00:16:59,052 --> 00:17:00,420
Aren't you interested?

248
00:17:01,154 --> 00:17:03,190
Yeah, I really don't understand.

249
00:17:03,223 --> 00:17:05,392
I mean, I thought you called me
here to give me an answer.

250
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:07,227
Why am I here?

251
00:17:07,662 --> 00:17:09,129
[coin flips]

252
00:17:10,532 --> 00:17:13,868
Julius Caesar was the first
Roman emperor to mint coins

253
00:17:13,902 --> 00:17:15,269
with his face on them.

254
00:17:15,302 --> 00:17:17,371
He wanted to forge his legend.

255
00:17:17,404 --> 00:17:22,175
He wanted to be talked about
from South Germania to Africa.

256
00:17:22,209 --> 00:17:24,244
Why do you think
that was, Forster?

257
00:17:25,178 --> 00:17:27,682
Because it was good
for business.

258
00:17:27,715 --> 00:17:30,752
In any case, the first emperor
was Octavian, sir.

259
00:17:30,785 --> 00:17:32,452
Caesar was a dictator.

260
